 ## Background
-VRPrior was introduced in the paper "VRP-UDF: Toward Unbiased Learning of Unsigned Distance Functions From Multi-View Images With Volume Rendering Priors" [S1]. It addresses limitations in previous differentiable renderers that used handcrafted equations (e.g., NeUDF [2], 2S-UDF [28]) which were biased and not 3D aware. The method builds on the idea of learnable neural rendering frameworks [66–68] and hierarchical volume sampling [69]. It was developed to provide a more robust and scalable way to map UDFs to opaque densities for alpha blending [S1].
+VRPrior was introduced in the paper "VRP-UDF: Toward Unbiased Learning of Unsigned Distance Functions From Multi-View Images With Volume Rendering Priors" [S1]. It addresses limitations in previous differentiable renderers that used handcrafted equations (e.g., NeUDF [2], 2S-UDF [28]) which were biased and not 3D aware [S1]. The method builds on the idea of learnable neural rendering frameworks [66–68] and hierarchical volume sampling [69] [S1]. It was developed to provide a more robust and scalable way to map UDFs to opaque densities for alpha blending [S1].
 
